WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.500
You can write Tailwind CSS directly in Lynx.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.667
@weapp-tailwindcss/lynx brings Tailwind CSS 4 to ReactLynx and Rspeedy.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.433
Change the padding and radius.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.767
Save, build, and reload.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.700
More space.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.833
Rounder photo corners.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.333
Now change blue to green.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.767
Save, build, and reload.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.200
The native card is green.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.367
Styles become CSS at build time and enter the native bundle.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.400
The same component code runs natively on iOS and Android.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.933
From generation and encoding to native runtime, every boundary has evidence.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.433
Open the Lynx integration docs and start building.
